{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-35693","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-53784","text":"Forge Semantic IR v1 — FROZEN"}]},{"id":"blk-35694","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53785","text":"*Status: "},{"id":"spn-53786","marks":["bold"],"text":"FROZEN"},{"id":"spn-53787","text":" (2026-07-21), per GPT-5.6 ruling. Profile: "},{"id":"spn-53788","marks":["code"],"text":"forge.world.core.v1"},{"id":"spn-53789","text":" — the "},{"id":"spn-53790","marks":["bold"],"text":"deterministic-circuit-world"},{"id":"spn-53791","text":" profile. This is the sanctioned lowering target for WRL Core 0.1.1. WRL surface text NEVER lowers directly to interaction-calculus text; it lowers to this IR, which lowers to TRVM facts/films/reductions.*"}]},{"id":"blk-35695","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53792","marks":["bold"],"text":"Scope statement (normative)."},{"id":"spn-53793","text":" IR v1 defines static deterministic signal graphs containing the five built-in roles, persistent numeric/pose state, bounded ADMIT claim state, and the two grounded topology relations. It does "},{"id":"spn-53794","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-53795","text":" define mailboxes, arbitrary actor behavior, dynamic topology, fragments, capabilities, supervision, or distributed settlement. Any construct outside this scope MUST produce a clear unsupported-feature diagnostic, never a speculative lowering."}]},{"id":"blk-35696","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53796","text":"Predecessor: "},{"id":"spn-53797","marks":["code"],"text":"FORGE_SEMANTIC_IR_v1_MEASURE.md"},{"id":"spn-53798","text":" (the pre-freeze measure). Frozen core: "},{"id":"spn-53799","marks":["code"],"text":"WRL_CORE_0.1.md"},{"id":"spn-53800","text":" (rev 0.1.1). This freeze resolves decisions D1–D5 as ruled."}]},{"id":"blk-35697","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-53801","text":"0. Three layers (D3)"}]},{"id":"blk-35698","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53802","text":"IR v1 is three artifacts with three lifetimes. They are never conflated."}]},{"id":"blk-35699","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"ArtifactIR (static)  +  RuntimeState (persistent)  +  EpochInput (per-epoch)\n    → RuntimeState'  +  Observables"},{"id":"blk-35700","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35702","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53803","marks":["bold"],"text":"Static artifact"},{"id":"spn-53804","text":" — durable topology + role configs + policy references + schema references. Content-addressed."}]}],"id":"blk-35701","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35704","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53805","marks":["bold"],"text":"Persistent runtime state"},{"id":"spn-53806","text":" — world state, claim facts, receipts, capacity-fault latches, clock/pose/rotor/fault state. Threads across epochs."}]}],"id":"blk-35703","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35706","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53807","marks":["bold"],"text":"Epoch input"},{"id":"spn-53808","text":" — the incoming claim batch (later: external / effect-wall observations)."}]}],"id":"blk-35705","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-35707","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53809","text":"Claim facts and receipts are "},{"id":"spn-53810","marks":["bold"],"text":"top-level runtime state"},{"id":"spn-53811","text":", not hidden inside a special actor. ADMIT's "},{"id":"spn-53812","marks":["italic"],"text":"policy identity"},{"id":"spn-53813","text":" is static; its "},{"id":"spn-53814","marks":["italic"],"text":"facts and receipts"},{"id":"spn-53815","text":" are runtime state; the incoming "},{"id":"spn-53816","marks":["italic"],"text":"claim batch"},{"id":"spn-53817","text":" is epoch input."}]},{"id":"blk-35708","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-53818","text":"1. Node envelope + five built-in roles (D1)"}]},{"id":"blk-35709","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53819","text":"One structural node envelope is frozen:"}]},{"id":"blk-35710","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"Node {\n    object_id\n    role                 ; one of the five closed role IDs below\n    static_config        ; role-specific frozen config\n    state_schema_ref     ; semantic state signature (see §3)\n    ports                ; frozen per-role port signature\n}"},{"id":"blk-35711","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53820","text":"The entire executable v1 role registry is these five (closed):"}]},{"id":"blk-35712","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-53821","text":"PulserDecl"}]},{"id":"blk-35713","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35715","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53822","marks":["bold"],"text":"static_config:"},{"id":"spn-53823","text":" clock mode "},{"id":"spn-53824","marks":["code"],"text":"(\"periodic\", period, phase)"},{"id":"spn-53825","text":" | "},{"id":"spn-53826","marks":["code"],"text":"(\"once\", epoch)"},{"id":"spn-53827","text":" (period ≥ 1, 0 ≤ phase < period, period < 1e9; epoch in [0,1e6))."}]}],"id":"blk-35714","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35717","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53828","marks":["bold"],"text":"ports:"},{"id":"spn-53829","text":" out "},{"id":"spn-53830","marks":["code"],"text":"sig_out"},{"id":"spn-53831","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-35716","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35719","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53832","marks":["bold"],"text":"state:"},{"id":"spn-53833","text":" clock state (see §3)."}]}],"id":"blk-35718","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35721","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53834","marks":["bold"],"text":"invariant:"},{"id":"spn-53835","text":" fires deterministically by clock mode; never data-dependent."}]}],"id":"blk-35720","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-35722","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-53836","text":"RelayDecl"}]},{"id":"blk-35723","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35725","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53837","marks":["bold"],"text":"static_config:"},{"id":"spn-53838","text":" none."}]}],"id":"blk-35724","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35727","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53839","marks":["bold"],"text":"ports:"},{"id":"spn-53840","text":" out "},{"id":"spn-53841","marks":["code"],"text":"sig_out"},{"id":"spn-53842","text":"; in "},{"id":"spn-53843","marks":["code"],"text":"sig_in"},{"id":"spn-53844","text":" (or-merge of incoming wires)."}]}],"id":"blk-35726","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35729","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53845","marks":["bold"],"text":"state:"},{"id":"spn-53846","text":" "},{"id":"spn-53847","marks":["code"],"text":"cur_out"},{"id":"spn-53848","text":", "},{"id":"spn-53849","marks":["code"],"text":"next_out"},{"id":"spn-53850","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-35728","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35731","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53851","marks":["bold"],"text":"invariant:"},{"id":"spn-53852","text":" "},{"id":"spn-53853","marks":["code"],"text":"next_out = OR(incoming .nxt)"},{"id":"spn-53854","text":"; "},{"id":"spn-53855","marks":["code"],"text":"cur_out' = next_out"},{"id":"spn-53856","text":" at commit."}]}],"id":"blk-35730","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-35732","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-53857","text":"DoorDecl"}]},{"id":"blk-35733","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35735","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53858","marks":["bold"],"text":"static_config:"},{"id":"spn-53859","text":" none."}]}],"id":"blk-35734","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35737","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53860","marks":["bold"],"text":"ports:"},{"id":"spn-53861","text":" in "},{"id":"spn-53862","marks":["code"],"text":"sig_in"},{"id":"spn-53863","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-35736","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35739","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53864","marks":["bold"],"text":"state:"},{"id":"spn-53865","text":" "},{"id":"spn-53866","marks":["code"],"text":"open"},{"id":"spn-53867","text":", "},{"id":"spn-53868","marks":["code"],"text":"next_open"},{"id":"spn-53869","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-35738","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35741","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53870","marks":["bold"],"text":"invariant:"},{"id":"spn-53871","text":" "},{"id":"spn-53872","marks":["code"],"text":"open' = next_open"},{"id":"spn-53873","text":"; "},{"id":"spn-53874","marks":["code"],"text":"next_open' = incoming wire "},{"id":"spn-53875","text":".nxt`."}]}],"id":"blk-35740","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-35742","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-53876","text":"SpinnerDecl"}]},{"id":"blk-35743","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35745","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53877","marks":["bold"],"text":"static_config:"},{"id":"spn-53878","text":" lane geometry "},{"id":"spn-53879","marks":["code"],"text":"(w, n)"},{"id":"spn-53880","text":", initial "},{"id":"spn-53881","marks":["code"],"text":"rotor4"},{"id":"spn-53882","text":", "},{"id":"spn-53883","marks":["code"],"text":"configurable"},{"id":"spn-53884","text":" permission (fixed | configurable)."}]}],"id":"blk-35744","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35747","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53885","marks":["bold"],"text":"ports:"},{"id":"spn-53886","text":" in "},{"id":"spn-53887","marks":["code"],"text":"sig_in"},{"id":"spn-53888","text":" (exactly one); out "},{"id":"spn-53889","marks":["code"],"text":"socket"},{"id":"spn-53890","text":" (exactly one)."}]}],"id":"blk-35746","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35749","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53891","marks":["bold"],"text":"state:"},{"id":"spn-53892","text":" "},{"id":"spn-53893","marks":["code"],"text":"rotor"},{"id":"spn-53894","text":" (Q-fixed lanes, runtime STATE)."}]}],"id":"blk-35748","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35751","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53895","marks":["bold"],"text":"invariant:"},{"id":"spn-53896","text":" exactly one sig-in + exactly one socket; fixed spinners REJECT runtime rotor writes (typed error); configurable accept "},{"id":"spn-53897","marks":["code"],"text":"SetRotor"},{"id":"spn-53898","text":" at COMMIT."}]}],"id":"blk-35750","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-35752","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-53899","text":"OrbDecl"}]},{"id":"blk-35753","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35755","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53900","marks":["bold"],"text":"static_config:"},{"id":"spn-53901","text":" none."}]}],"id":"blk-35754","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35757","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53902","marks":["bold"],"text":"ports:"},{"id":"spn-53903","text":" in "},{"id":"spn-53904","marks":["code"],"text":"pose"},{"id":"spn-53905","text":" (via socket)."}]}],"id":"blk-35756","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35759","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53906","marks":["bold"],"text":"state:"},{"id":"spn-53907","text":" "},{"id":"spn-53908","marks":["code"],"text":"pose4"},{"id":"spn-53909","text":", sticky "},{"id":"spn-53910","marks":["code"],"text":"numeric_fault"},{"id":"spn-53911","text":" bit."}]}],"id":"blk-35758","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35761","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53912","marks":["bold"],"text":"invariant:"},{"id":"spn-53913","text":" controller exclusivity (≤ 1 socket); "},{"id":"spn-53914","marks":["code"],"text":"numeric_fault' = fault_base OR current_overflow"},{"id":"spn-53915","text":" where "},{"id":"spn-53916","marks":["code"],"text":"fault_base = 0 if ResetFault else old"},{"id":"spn-53917","text":" (a reset cannot hide a same-epoch overflow)."}]}],"id":"blk-35760","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-35762","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53918","marks":["bold"],"text":"Frozen:"},{"id":"spn-53919","text":" node envelope, the five role IDs, their config/port/state signatures, their invariants. "},{"id":"spn-53920","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not frozen:"},{"id":"spn-53921","text":" user-defined behaviors, mailboxes, supervision, generic behavior tables, dynamic role loading, the physical IC encoding of each state. New built-in roles are additive "},{"id":"spn-53922","marks":["bold"],"text":"v1.x"},{"id":"spn-53923","text":"; a general actor-behavior system stays Experimental."}]},{"id":"blk-35763","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-53924","text":"2. Edge vocabulary (D2)"}]},{"id":"blk-35764","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53925","text":"Exactly two "},{"id":"spn-53926","marks":["bold"],"text":"structural topology edges"},{"id":"spn-53927","text":" are frozen:"}]},{"id":"blk-35765","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"SignalWireDecl    { src.sig_out → dst.sig_in }   ; dst ∈ {Door, Relay, Spinner}\nSocketControlDecl { spinner.socket → orb.pose }"},{"id":"blk-35766","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53928","text":"Legal pairs: "},{"id":"spn-53929","marks":["code"],"text":"(sig_out, sig_in)"},{"id":"spn-53930","text":", "},{"id":"spn-53931","marks":["code"],"text":"(socket, pose)"},{"id":"spn-53932","text":". Any other edge variant MUST fail validation."}]},{"id":"blk-35767","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53933","marks":["bold"],"text":"Graph edges are not transition classes."},{"id":"spn-53934","text":" These are NOT structural edge kinds in v1:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-35769","spans":[{"id":"spn-53935","text":"WRL texture"}]},{"id":"blk-35770","spans":[{"id":"spn-53936","text":"IR v1 status"}]}],"id":"blk-35768","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-35771","spans":[{"id":"spn-53937","text":"Solid "},{"id":"spn-53938","marks":["code"],"text":"--"}]},{"id":"blk-35772","spans":[{"id":"spn-53939","text":"executable through "},{"id":"spn-53940","marks":["code"],"text":"SignalWire"}]}],[{"id":"blk-35773","spans":[{"id":"spn-53941","text":"Async "},{"id":"spn-53942","marks":["code"],"text":"~~"}]},{"id":"blk-35774","spans":[{"id":"spn-53943","text":"reserved in WRL, "},{"id":"spn-53944","marks":["bold"],"text":"absent"},{"id":"spn-53945","text":" from IR v1 (no placeholder node)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-35775","spans":[{"id":"spn-53946","text":"Verified "},{"id":"spn-53947","marks":["code"],"text":"=="}]},{"id":"blk-35776","spans":[{"id":"spn-53948","text":"acceptance machinery grounded; route construct "},{"id":"spn-53949","marks":["bold"],"text":"absent"}]}],[{"id":"blk-35777","spans":[{"id":"spn-53950","text":"Fault "},{"id":"spn-53951","marks":["code"],"text":"!!"}]},{"id":"blk-35778","spans":[{"id":"spn-53952","text":"fault state grounded; route/supervision construct "},{"id":"spn-53953","marks":["bold"],"text":"absent"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-35779","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53954","text":"A numeric-fault latch is "},{"id":"spn-53955","marks":["italic"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-53956","text":" the lowering of a "},{"id":"spn-53957","marks":["code"],"text":"!!fault!!>"},{"id":"spn-53958","text":" route; an acceptance receipt is "},{"id":"spn-53959","marks":["italic"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-53960","text":" a complete lowering of a "},{"id":"spn-53961","marks":["code"],"text":"==verified==>"},{"id":"spn-53962","text":" route. Reserved WRL syntax needs no placeholder canonical IR node."}]},{"id":"blk-35780","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-53963","text":"3. State schema — semantic vs backend (D4)"}]},{"id":"blk-35781","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53964","text":"IR v1 freezes "},{"id":"spn-53965","marks":["bold"],"text":"semantic signatures"},{"id":"spn-53966","text":"; it excludes "},{"id":"spn-53967","marks":["bold"],"text":"backend encodings"},{"id":"spn-53968","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-35782","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53969","marks":["bold"],"text":"Semantic (in the artifact or a referenced policy/schema):"},{"id":"spn-53970","text":" signedness; lane width; fractional bits; numeric-policy identity; saturation behavior; rounding behavior; sticky-fault behavior; fixed-vs-configurable permission; fact/receipt capacity (when exhaustion is observable); rotor & pose lane counts; claim & receipt field meanings."}]},{"id":"blk-35783","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53971","marks":["bold"],"text":"Backend (excluded — belongs to a lowering profile):"},{"id":"spn-53972","text":" Scott encoding; tuple nesting; DUP labels; one-hot vs binary clock counter; packed-word layout; IC variable names; native struct padding; CUDA memory layout."}]},{"id":"blk-35784","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53973","marks":["bold"],"text":"Identity split (frozen):"}]},{"id":"blk-35785","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"SemanticArtifactID = hash( canonical Forge IR + semantic policy references )\nBackendArtifactID  = hash( SemanticArtifactID + lowering profile + compiler hash + backend representation )"},{"id":"blk-35786","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53974","text":"Changing one-hot → binary changes the "},{"id":"spn-53975","marks":["bold"],"text":"BackendArtifactID"},{"id":"spn-53976","text":" only (not the world identity or WorldFrame). Changing Q32.32 → Q16.16 changes the "},{"id":"spn-53977","marks":["bold"],"text":"SemanticArtifactID"},{"id":"spn-53978","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-35787","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-53979","text":"4. Frozen top-level forms"}]},{"id":"blk-35788","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"ForgeSemanticArtifactV1 {\n    ir_version\n    profile_id                 ; \"forge.world.core.v1\" (deterministic-circuit-world)\n    semantic_policies {\n        rulepack_id\n        numeric_policy_ids\n        admit_policy_id        ; e.g. admit_candidate_min_firstreceipt_v1\n        film_schema_id\n    }\n    schemas {\n        runtime_state_schema\n        epoch_input_schema\n        observable_schema\n    }\n    objects: [ PulserDecl, RelayDecl, DoorDecl, SpinnerDecl, OrbDecl ]\n    edges:   [ SignalWireDecl, SocketControlDecl ]\n    initial_state\n}\n\nRuntimeStateV1 {\n    epoch\n    clock_states\n    signal_states\n    door_states\n    relay_states\n    spinner_rotors\n    orb_poses\n    numeric_faults\n    claim_facts\n    acceptance_receipts\n    capacity_faults\n}\n\nEpochInputV1 { claim_batch }          ; ClaimBatch of SetRotor|ResetFault envelopes\n\nEpochResultV1 { runtime_state, world_frame, ledger_entries }"},{"id":"blk-35789","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-53980","text":"5. Transition law (frozen)"}]},{"id":"blk-35790","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53981","text":"Per epoch the transition is the WRL Core 0.1.1 cycle:"}]},{"id":"blk-35791","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"OBSERVE → ACCEPT → MAP → COMMIT → REACT → FILM"},{"id":"blk-35792","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53982","text":"For claim-free epochs OBSERVE/ACCEPT/MAP degenerate to identity but remain in the model. COMMIT applies MAP'd controls (SetRotor writes + fault resets) to owned cells; REACT runs the deterministic within-period token cascade to fixpoint and latches overflow; FILM emits the "},{"id":"spn-53983","marks":["bold"],"text":"WorldFrame"},{"id":"spn-53984","text":" (physical, Film v0.6 family) + "},{"id":"spn-53985","marks":["bold"],"text":"EventLedger"},{"id":"spn-53986","text":" entries (claim-aware, Film v0.7 family). Canonical ordering is policy-pinned (the ADMIT profile pins "},{"id":"spn-53987","marks":["code"],"text":"CandidateKey"},{"id":"spn-53988","text":")."}]},{"id":"blk-35793","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-53989","text":"6. Versioning (D5)"}]},{"id":"blk-35794","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35796","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53990","marks":["bold"],"text":"v1"},{"id":"spn-53991","text":" freezes on the grounded "},{"id":"spn-53992","marks":["code"],"text":"deterministic-circuit-world"},{"id":"spn-53993","text":" profile — sufficient evidence exists (multiple clock modes, randomized topologies, fan-in/out, cycles, multiple controllers, dynamic rotors, persistent multi-epoch state, claims/receipts, fault reset, pose authority, native+reference reducers). It does "},{"id":"spn-53994","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-53995","text":" claim to be the universal final Forge IR."}]}],"id":"blk-35795","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35798","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53996","marks":["bold"],"text":"v1.1"},{"id":"spn-53997","text":" — additive role/field variants when a second world family arrives."}]}],"id":"blk-35797","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35800","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53998","marks":["bold"],"text":"v1.x"},{"id":"spn-53999","text":" — additive optional feature declarations."}]}],"id":"blk-35799","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35802","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54000","marks":["bold"],"text":"v2"},{"id":"spn-54001","text":" — any change to the meaning of an existing field. A second implementation must NOT silently reinterpret v1 fields."}]}],"id":"blk-35801","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-35803","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-54002","text":"7. First WRL vertical slice (what the compiler supports)"}]},{"id":"blk-35804","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"WRL Core text/canvas → canonical WRL graph → Forge Semantic IR v1\n    → current Fixture adapter → TRVM compiler → ic_ref / ic32 → Film v0.7"},{"id":"blk-35805","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54003","text":"Supported: Pulser, Relay, Door, Spinner, Orb; signal wires; socket control; fixed-point policy declarations; "},{"id":"spn-54004","marks":["code"],"text":"SetRotor"},{"id":"spn-54005","text":"; "},{"id":"spn-54006","marks":["code"],"text":"ResetFault"},{"id":"spn-54007","text":"; a fixed number of periods. Everything else → clear unsupported-feature diagnostic."}]},{"id":"blk-35806","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-54008","text":"8. Conformance (what IR v1 does NOT define)"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-35808","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54009","text":"IR v1 defines static deterministic signal graphs containing the five built-in roles, persistent numeric pose state, bounded ADMIT claim state, and the two grounded topology relations. It does not define mailboxes, arbitrary actor behavior, dynamic topology, fragments, capabilities, supervision, or distributed settlement."}]}],"id":"blk-35807","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-35809","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-54010","text":"D1–D5 resolution"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-35811","spans":[{"id":"spn-54011","text":"Decision"}]},{"id":"blk-35812","spans":[{"id":"spn-54012","text":"Ruling (frozen)"}]}],"id":"blk-35810","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-35813","spans":[{"id":"spn-54013","text":"D1 node vocabulary"}]},{"id":"blk-35814","spans":[{"id":"spn-54014","text":"stable node envelope + five closed built-in roles"}]}],[{"id":"blk-35815","spans":[{"id":"spn-54015","text":"D2 edge vocabulary"}]},{"id":"blk-35816","spans":[{"id":"spn-54016","text":"two structural edge kinds only; async/fault/verified are transition-class reserved, not edges"}]}],[{"id":"blk-35817","spans":[{"id":"spn-54017","text":"D3 ADMIT"}]},{"id":"blk-35818","spans":[{"id":"spn-54018","text":"static policy + top-level runtime ClaimState + separate EpochInput (three layers)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-35819","spans":[{"id":"spn-54019","text":"D4 state schema"}]},{"id":"blk-35820","spans":[{"id":"spn-54020","text":"semantic signature frozen in artifact; physical representation excluded to backend profile; Semantic/Backend artifact-ID split"}]}],[{"id":"blk-35821","spans":[{"id":"spn-54021","text":"D5 freeze timing"}]},{"id":"blk-35822","spans":[{"id":"spn-54022","text":"freeze now as restricted "},{"id":"spn-54023","marks":["code"],"text":"deterministic-circuit-world"},{"id":"spn-54024","text":" profile; v1.1 additive, v2 semantic"}]}]]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaierasvhip3qsqujwylyv4eigevtwumshq34jc4lbdokdcfmtggabin3a","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}